    {
      "id": "set-max-decimal-places",
      "name": "SetMaxDecimalPlaces",
      "category": "writer",
      "signature": "SetMaxDecimalPlaces(Target, Max Decimal Places)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "Writer*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Max Decimal Places",
          "type": "Int"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "!\nThis setting truncates the output with specified number of decimal places.\nFor example,\n\\code\nwriter.SetMaxDecimalPlaces(3);\nwriter.StartArray();\nwriter.Double(0.12345);                 // \"0.123\"\nwriter.Double(0.0001);                  // \"0.0\"\nwriter.Double(1.234567890123456e30);    // \"1.234567890123456e30\" (do not truncate significand for positive exponent)\nwriter.Double(1.23e-4);                 // \"0.0\"                  (do truncate significand for negative exponent)\nwriter.EndArray();\n\\endcode\nThe default setting does not truncate any decimal places. You can restore to this setting by calling\n\\code\nwriter.SetMaxDecimalPlaces(Writer::kDefaultMaxDecimalPlaces);\n\\endcode"
    },
